  "verification": {
    "status": "software-preview",
    "hardware_verified": false,
    "notes": [
      "Native Python GTK/Cairo runtime; common/ provides shared drawing, theme, telemetry and scene definitions; scenes/ owns each scenario.",
      "Automotive: dedicated dual-round drive-speed and engine-status panels; demo-only linked speed/gear/RPM/temperature/fuel/voltage/trip data.",
      "Automotive dual480 accepts 60Hz and the observed native ~62.825226Hz without changing hardware modes. Its physical scene acceptance is pending.",
      "Flight/industrial/mixed commands remain compatible; prior physical flight evidence is historical and does not certify the new automotive scene.",
      "No touch support or real OBD/vehicle control. Same-content is declared by round music/lighting/clock, square retail/meeting/parcel and their showcases; existing instrument/showcase views remain different-content.",
      "PC-monitor scene: simulated linked CPU/GPU workloads or explicit JSON from a monitored computer; missing sensors are unavailable, not invented or replaced with local Pi metrics.",
      "Product showcase is an independent demo-only playlist: flight, automotive, PC-monitor; title3s/effect10s; one39s loop in one surface. No live data or device control.",
      "Music scenes use simulated beat envelopes with no audio capture/output. SBS copies one raster to two round regions; clone uses one square input duplicated by the hardware board. Physical acceptance is separate from software checks.",
      "Same-content showcase: simulated music, RGB light and demo time/weather;3s identical intros +10s effects,39s loop. Default hardware clone or explicit SBS. No audio, network weather or physical lighting control.",
      "Version0.10.0 groups canonical code by same/different content and shape. Square same-content uses retail promotions, room status and parcel pickup; all simulated,60Hz mappings, no physical square acceptance. Legacy command/import adapters preserve IDs. Local-only validation; no Pi deployment this release."
    ],
